Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1789865999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The window high 2771.00 (1787270400000) is 25 bars old and untouched; price is still below the 2680.00 range high on a closing basis, so the breakout leg remains an attempt inside the range, not accepted structure.", "The last bar was rejected at 2700.00, leaving an upper tail of about 67 points, and the prior 2680.00 attempt (1789084800000) closed roughly 165 points below its high; the same zone has produced two visible sellers' reactions, an incipient double top.", "1789430400000 is a wide bear bar (open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10) that erased several bull closes in one bar, showing two-sided trade with bears still able to produce strong bars inside the range.", "A 29-bar overlapping range after a near-vertical spike is equally consistent with a climactic spike followed by distribution; the spike's 2771.00 tail bar closed only at 2515.30, well below its high."], "evidence_for": ["The most recent close 2632.98 is the highest close of the supplied 120 bars, and the last two bars are consecutive bull bars that take out the prior six bars' highs and the 2557.46 inner ceiling.", "Whole-window structure is a bull sequence of higher swing lows (1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1551.60 -> 1694.74 -> 2357.18) with the 2358.62 low (1789430400000) holding above 2357.18, so the 29-bar sideways stretch follows a strong bull spike and reads as a bull flag rather than a completed top.", "Range pullbacks have been shallow relative to the 1905.63-2771.00 spike: most range closes stay above the spike's midpoint near 2338, and each push down to the 2357-2395 area has been bought back into the 2440-2530 zone.", "Each successive upper test has closed higher (2514.72 at 1789084800000 versus 2632.98 at 1789776000000), i.e. sellers at 2680-2700 have not produced a lower close or an accepted break back down."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed D1 bars, first open 2066.43 (1779494400000), last bar open 2612.03 / high 2700 / low 2604.75 / close 2632.98 (close_time_ms 1789862399999).", "Bars 1-15 of the window decline from high 2143.61 (1779494400000) to low 1368.42 (1780704000000); the 1780704000000 bar has range 1368.42-1599.27 and closes 1568.55 in the upper part of that range with a long lower tail.", "Higher lows follow the 1368.42 low: 1512.91 (1782432000000), 1551.60 (1782777600000), 1694.74 (1783296000000); rising highs reach 1959.37 (1785024000000), then ~12 bars overlap between roughly 1820 and 1960 (1785456000000-1787011200000).", "Three-bar bull spike from 1905.63 to 2771.00: opens/closes 1916.51/2252.16, 2252.20/2326.32, 2326.31/2515.30 at 1787097600000, 1787184000000, 1787270400000; the 2771.00 high leaves a large upper tail on the third bar.", "Since 1787356800000 the market has been sideways: 29 bars between low 2357.18 (1788307200000) and spike highs 2680.00 (1789084800000) and 2700.00 (1789776000000), with most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540 and an inner ceiling at 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "Two separate upside spike attempts above that inner ceiling: 1789084800000 (open 2436.83, high 2680.00, close 2514.72, upper tail ~165) and 1789689600000-1789776000000 (close 2612.02, then high 2700.00 with close 2632.98, upper tail ~67).", "1789430400000 is a large bear bar inside the same range: open 2513.91, low 2358.62, close 2397.10, i.e. a wide body closing near its low.", "The last close 2632.98 is the highest close in the supplied 120-bar window, and the 2700.00 high is still below the window high 2771.00."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Opening bear leg of the window: 15 bars of lower highs and lower lows from 2143.61 into an accelerating sell-off that reaches 1368.42 (1780704000000), where the bar closes at 1568.55 in the upper 72% of its 1368.42-1599.27 range, a long-lower-tail reversal bar.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1779494400000, "upper_boundary": "2143.61"}, {"description": "Recovery and uptrend from the 1368.42 low: higher lows at 1512.91 (1782432000000) and 1551.60 (1782777600000) with rising highs into 1959.37 (1785024000000), followed by an overlapping ~1820-1960 pause (1785456000000-1787011200000) that holds well above the 1368.42 origin.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1959.37"}, {"description": "Three-bar bull spike: bars at 1787097600000, 1787184000000 and 1787270400000 run from 1905.63 to 2771.00 with closes 2252.16, 2326.32 and 2515.30; the 2771.00 extreme is a spike high with a large upper tail and has not been retested.", "end_time_ms": 1787270400000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Trading range after the spike: 29 bars from 1787356800000 to the last bar, bounded by 2357.18 (1788307200000) and the 2680.00 spike high (1789084800000), with heavy overlap, most closes between roughly 2390 and 2540, and an inner ceiling near 2557.46 (1787788800000).", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two upside spike attempts into the same 2680.00-2700.00 area (1789084800000: high 2680.00, close 2514.72; 1789776000000: high 2700.00, close 2632.98) separated by a sell-off to 2358.62 (1789430400000). The pair is a possible double top at the range high, though the second attempt closes 118 points higher than the first.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789084800000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Two-bar bull leg / breakout attempt: 1789689600000 (open 2446.22, high 2643.52, close 2612.02) and 1789776000000 (open 2612.03, high 2700.00, low 2604.75, close 2632.98). Price lifts above the 2557.46 inner ceiling and prints the window's highest close, but has not yet closed above the 2680.00 range high.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Acceptance above the 2680.00 range high, e.g. a close above it followed by another bar closing above 2700.00, would confirm the range breakout and support the bull-trend / breakout-spike read.", "A close back below 2557.46 and into the 2390-2540 range body would negate the breakout attempt and restore an intact trading range between 2357.18 and 2680.00.", "A close below 2357.18 would be a bear breakout from the 29-bar range and would shift the structural read away from the bull flag toward a bear or transition classification.", "Failure to exceed 2680.00 over the next few bars while forming a lower high below 2700.00 would leave the two-sided/double-top interpretation as the strongest alternative and reduce Always-In relevance to low."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1789862399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest earlier bull spike in the window (1789128000000) was not accepted: its entire 235.81-point range was given back and price closed below 2411.04, so a strong bar in this window has recently marked a trap rather than a trend start.", "The newest high is only a wick: bar 1789804800000 reached 2700 but closed 2638.49 (upper tail about 61.5), the highest close since is 2640.01 (1789819200000), and no close in the last four bars exceeds 2680.", "An earlier test of comparable resistance failed the same way: bar 1789416000000 spiked to 2609.02 and closed 2514.07 near its low, which preceded the 322-point drop to 2358.62.", "The window as a whole is two-sided with large legs both ways (up legs of roughly 180, 269 and 342 points against down legs of roughly 126 and 322 points), which is equally consistent with a large trading range between 2357.18/2358.62 and 2680/2700 rather than a sustained trend.", "The last seven bars have shrinking ranges and stay under 2658.79 (1789833600000 high); a tight range at the top of a leg is how both a pause in a trend and a range top begin, so the breakout is still unconfirmed."], "evidence_for": ["Swing progression in the last 26 bars is bullish: five rising lows since 1789488000000 and successively higher highs, the pattern expected of a bull leg rather than a range.", "Two consecutive strong bull bars (1789732800000 close 2578.6; 1789747200000 close 2636.28) forced price above the mid-window range top 2528.8/2537.57, and all nine closes from 1789732800000 onward hold above that boundary, i.e. acceptance rather than a one-bar poke.", "At the larger degree the sequence is also bullish: 2358.62 is a marginal higher low versus 2357.18, and 2700 is a higher high versus the 2680 spike high.", "Pullbacks inside the current leg stayed small relative to its size (for example 2643.52 to 2604.75, about 11 percent of the 2358.62-to-2700 advance), so no completed two-legged reversal has formed yet."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window spans 120 closed H4 bars from 1788134400000 (open 2407) to 1789848000000 (close 2632.98): net higher, with window low 2357.18 (bar 1788336000000) and window high 2700 (bar 1789804800000).", "Bars 1788537600000-1789127999999 form a two-sided range of overlapping bars with closes mostly 2460-2530, bounded by 2411.04 (1789041600000 low) and 2528.8 (1788739200000 high).", "Bar 1789128000000 is a spike bar (open 2457.12, high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52; range 235.81) that broke above that range, then gave the entire range back: price closed below 2411.04 and reached 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000).", "The last 26 bars are a directional leg with rising lows 2358.62, 2370.54 (1789574400000), 2435.71 (1789646400000), 2486.12 (1789718400000), 2604.75 (1789776000000) and rising highs 2438.47 (1789603200000), 2481.66 (1789646400000), 2519.81 (1789718400000), 2643.52 (1789747200000), 2700 (1789804800000).", "Strongest bars of that leg are 1789732800000 (open 2507.15, close 2578.6) and 1789747200000 (open 2579.97, close 2636.28), which closed well above the mid-window range top 2528.8 and above 2537.57 (1788508800000 high).", "The last seven bars (1789761600000-1789862399999) are a tight range 2604.75-2700; closes are 2612.02 to 2640.01, no close exceeds 2680, and bar 1789804800000 poked 2700 but closed 2638.49 with a roughly 61.5-point upper tail."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Mid-window two-sided range after the 1788436800000 bull spike: repeated overlap, closes largely between 2460 and 2530, capped by 2528.8 and floored by 2411.04.", "end_time_ms": 1789127999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2411.04", "start_time_ms": 1788537600000, "upper_boundary": "2528.8"}, {"description": "Spike bar 1789128000000 (open 2457.12, high 2680, low 2444.19, close 2555.52) broke the mid-window range; not accepted, as the market retraced through the range floor to 2358.62 over the following 25 bars.", "end_time_ms": 1789502399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789128000000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Recent bull leg from 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000) up to 2700, containing higher lows 2370.54, 2435.71, 2486.12, 2604.75 and higher highs up to 2643.52; the leg is a grind with overlapping bars for most of its length and two strong trend bars near its end.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Seven-bar tight range at the high (1789761600000-1789862399999) between 2604.75 and the 2700 spike high; the 2700 poke in bar 1789804800000 closed 2638.49, and no subsequent close exceeds 2680.", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2604.75", "start_time_ms": 1789761600000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}, {"description": "Window extremes: rough double bottom at 2357.18 (bar 1788336000000) and 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000), with the 2700 high (bar 1789804800000) marginally above the earlier spike high 2680 (bar 1789128000000).", "end_time_ms": 1789862399999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1788336000000, "upper_boundary": "2700"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["A close above 2700, or two consecutive closes above 2680, would confirm acceptance of a higher-high breakout and support continuation of the bull trend.", "A bear bar closing below the tight range low 2604.75 would end the chain of higher lows, flip Always-In to short and mark the current leg as a completed bull leg.", "A close below 2486.12 (1789718400000 low) would break the higher-low sequence of the recent leg and shift the read toward a larger two-sided range.", "Continued overlapping bars between 2604.75 and 2643.52 with no close above 2658.79 would keep the breakout unconfirmed and increase the odds that the window is a range top rather than trend continuation."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2513.88", "close_time_ms": 1789437599999, "high": "2517.42", "low": "2507.12", "open": "2514.53", "open_time_ms": 1789434000000, "volume": "2090459.722"}, {"close": "2511.01", "close_time_ms": 1789441199999, "high": "2517.53", "low": "2509.21", "open": "2513.66", "open_time_ms": 178943760